SUMMARY:Cyber + Global Policy in Washington\, DC: Study Away Open House
DESCRIPTION:In Washington\, D.C.\, policy is the new perimeter. Join Isak
  Nti-Asare&#160\;and Katherine Ntiamoah for a targeted "come and go" lunc
 h regarding the Washington&#160\;D.C. Global Policy Program. (https://hls
 .indiana.edu/careers/dc-global-policy-program/index.html)This session is 
 designed specifically for students in the Cybersecurity and Global Policy
  joint degree.  Whether your goal is a residency at CISA\, the Department
  of Justice\, the NSA\, or a private sector tech policy firm\, this is yo
 ur chance to see how the D.C. residency functions as a professional launc
 hpad for your technical expertise.What to Expect:The Cyber Pipeline: Guid
 ance on identifying and securing D.C. internship placements that value th
 e Luddy/HLS joint-degree background.    Day One Readiness: How our "trade
 craft" model prepares you to brief officials on complex cyber threats fro
 m your first day in the capital.    The Roadmap: A technical walkthrough 
 of the October 15 application deadline and the 2027 semester start date f
 or the Spring cohort.      We know your schedule is tight. Drop in for 20
  minutes to grab lunch and the "HLS D.C. Guide"\, or stay for the full di
 scussion.  &#160\;  Experience the Washington D.C. Global Policy Program 
 (https://hls.indiana.edu/careers/dc-global-policy-program/index.html)Appl
 ication Here:https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24aW (ht
 tps://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24aW)  &#160\;  Lunch P
 rovided
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-path-to-node="13">  In Washington\, 
 D.C.\, policy is the new perimeter. Join <strong data-path-to-node="13" d
 ata-index-in-node="55">Isak Nti-Asare</strong>&#160\;and <strong data-pat
 h-to-node="13" data-index-in-node="129">Katherine Ntiamoah</strong> for a
  targeted "come and go" lunch regarding the <strong><a href="https://hls.
 indiana.edu/careers/dc-global-policy-program/index.html">Washington&#160\
 ;D.C. Global Policy Program.</a></strong></p><p data-path-to-node="13"><e
 m><strong><img src="https://partners.wsj.com/indiana-university/the-next-
 generation-of-business/wp-content/uploads/sites/1266/2025/02/INDIANA-UNIV
 ERSITY_SuppliedArticle_Hero.jpg" alt="Paid Program: Securing Our Cyber Fu
 ture" loading="lazy"/></strong></em></p><p data-path-to-node="14"><em><st
 rong>This session is designed specifically for students in the Cybersecur
 ity and Global Policy joint degree.</strong></em></p><p data-path-to-node
 ="14">  Whether your goal is a residency at CISA\, the Department of Just
 ice\, the NSA\, or a private sector tech policy firm\, this is your chanc
 e to see how the D.C. residency functions as a professional launchpad for
  your technical expertise.</p><p data-path-to-node="15"><strong data-path
 -to-node="15" data-index-in-node="0">What to Expect:</strong></p><ul data
 -path-to-node="16"><li><p data-path-to-node="16\,0\,0"><strong data-path-
